==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lowkey]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 2.67~6 seconds<sup>80f~180f</sup>.
**20 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 2.67~6 seconds<sup>80f~180f</sup>.
**1 [[Othom]] spawns.
**2 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
**2 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The only difficult part of the stage is surviving the first wave. However, since nearly all of the enemies are [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], just equipping some [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating cats]] makes the stage trivial.

Use 3 meatshields, [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] (for the initial wave if it does not have the [[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]] [[Talents|Talent]], for the entire stage if it does), [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan]] for killing the Lowkey, (not strictly required) and 2-3 long-ranged attackers like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Schoolbus Nyandam]] and/or [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]. Just stall the Relic Doges, build up your money, and attack the enemy base. Eventually, the Othom will die, and you can use Manic Jamiera and/or Octopus Cat to kill the Lowkey. You don't need to stack Cyberpunk Cats, but you can if you are unable beat the stage without it.

A high-level, curse-immune Octopus can almost guarantee a success. Other helpful cats are [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], etc.

==Trivia==
*Despite the name, there are no camels (i.e. [[Camelle]] variants) in this stage.

